\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Proved a frame-invariant screen-Jacobi determinant criterion and checked constant-curvature and Riccati limits. No Kerr caustic rays, sheets or stability classification is computed.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied complete definition, catalogue wording, scope qualifications and source list for this canonical ID. The original-source citations are inherited as supplied references; no fresh primary-source or novelty search was performed for this attempt. No current open-status claim is inferred from this calculation.

\paragraph{An invariant transverse-Jacobi criterion.}Along a chosen null geodesic with affine parameter \(s\), suppose the screen Jacobi equation is \(A''(s)+\mathcal R(s)A(s)=0\), where \(A\) is a real \(2\times2\) matrix, \(A(0)=0\), \(A'(0)=I\), and \(\mathcal R\) is a continuous symmetric optical tidal matrix in a parallel orthonormal screen frame. A nonzero initial screen vector \(v\) produces Jacobi field \(A(s)v\); consequently a conjugate point at \(s>0\) is exactly \(\det A(s)=0\). Orthogonal changes of endpoint screen frames multiply \(A\) on the left and right by invertible matrices, preserving the zero set of the determinant.
\paragraph{Exact curvature tests.}For \(\mathcal R=0\), \(A=sI\), with no positive conjugate point. For \(\mathcal R=\kappa I\), \(\kappa>0\), \(A=\sin(\sqrt\kappa s)I/\sqrt\kappa\), and the first is \(\pi/\sqrt\kappa\). For negative \(\kappa\), the hyperbolic-sine solution has none. Wherever \(A\) is invertible, \(B=A'A^{-1}\) satisfies \(B'+B^2+\mathcal R=0\), by direct differentiation. Its trace is the logarithmic derivative \((\det A)'/\det A\), linking area expansion to the caustic criterion.
\paragraph{Gap.}This ODE certificate identifies what to compute, but no Kerr ray, optical tidal matrix or conjugate location is evaluated. The constant-curvature tests are not Kerr substitutes. Higher-order/near-observer/off-equatorial sheets, astroid formation, stability under a specified metric perturbation class, optical terminology and the lightlike character of stable sheets remain unresolved. The first missing step is a controlled Kerr Jacobi integration and endpoint-map analysis; no plotting or numerical verification is claimed.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked Jacobi initial data, determinant criterion, frame invariance, zero/positive/negative constant curvature and Riccati trace sign. This was an LLM adversarial audit, not independent human verification; no theorem prover was used. Prompts A then B applied to this ID: Checked Jacobi initial data, determinant criterion, frame invariance, zero/positive/negative constant curvature and Riccati trace sign. Scope remains limited: Obtain controlled Kerr null-geodesic and Jacobi solutions, then analyze endpoint-map singularities in a defined stability class.

Coordinator checked the screen Jacobi determinant criterion, constant-curvature solutions and Riccati/log-determinant identities. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local shell used to read supplied files and serialize this manuscript; mathematics derived symbolically in the text, with no numerical experiment or formal proof assistant. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Obtain controlled Kerr null-geodesic and Jacobi solutions, then analyze endpoint-map singularities in a defined stability class.

